  "title": "82: al-Infetaar الإنفطار",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاِذَا السَّمَآءُ انْفَطَرَتْۙ‏(1)\nEZAS SAMAAA-UN FATARAT.\nWhen the Sky is cleft asunder; \nوَاِذَا الْكَوَاكِبُ انْتَثَرَتْۙ‏(2)\nWA EZAL KAWAAKEBUN TASARAT.\nWhen the Stars are scattered; \nوَاِذَا الْبِحَارُ فُجِّرَتْۙ‏(3)\nWA EZAL BEHAARO FUJJERAT.\nWhen the Oceans are suffered to burst forth; \nوَاِذَا الْقُبُوْرُ بُعْثِرَتْۙ‏(4)\nWA EZAL QOBOORO BO’SERAT.\nAnd when the Graves are turned upside down;- \nعَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّا قَدَّمَتْ وَاَخَّرَتْؕ‏(5)\nA’LEMAT NAFSUM MAA QADDAMAT WA AKHKHARAT.\n(Then) shall each soul know what it hath sent forward and (what it hath) kept back. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْاِنْسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيْمِۙ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL INSAANO MAA GHARRAKA BE-RABBEKAL KAREEMIL.\nO man! What has seduced thee from thy Lord Most Beneficent? \nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَكَ فَسَوّٰٮكَ فَعَدَلَكَۙ‏(7)\nLAZEE KHALAQAKA FA-SAWWAAKA FA-A’DALAKA.\nHim Who created thee. Fashioned thee in due proportion, and gave thee a just bias; \nفِىْۤ اَىِّ صُوْرَةٍ مَّا شَآءَ رَكَّبَكَؕ‏(8)\nFEE AYYE SOORATIM MAA SHAAA-A RAKKABAK.\nIn whatever Form He wills, does He put thee together. \nكَلَّا بَلْ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ بِالدِّيْنِۙ‏(9)\nKALLAA BAL TOKAZZEBOONA BID-DEENE.\nNay! But ye do reject Right and Judgment! \nوَاِنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ لَحٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWA INNA A’LAYKUM LA-HAAFEZEENA.\nBut verily over you (are appointed angels) to protect you,- \nكِرَامًا كَاتِبِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nKERAAMAN KAATEBEENA.\nKind and honourable,- Writing down (your deeds): \nيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(12)\nYA’LAMOONA MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nThey know (and understand) all that ye do. \nاِنَّ الْاَبْرَارَ لَفِىْ نَعِيْمٍۚ‏(13)\nINNAL ABRAARA LAFEE NA-E’EM.\nAs for the Righteous, they will be in bliss; \nوَاِنَّ الْفُجَّارَ لَفِىْ جَحِيْمٍ ۚۖ‏(14)\nWA INNAL FUJJAARA LAFEE JAHEEMIN-Y.\nAnd the Wicked - they will be in the Fire, \nيَّصْلَوْنَهَا يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِ‏(15)\nYASLAWNAHAA YAWMAD DEEN.\nWhich they will enter on the Day of Judgment, \nوَمَا هُمْ عَنْهَا بِغَآئِبِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nWA MAA HUM A’NHAA BE-GHAAA-EBEEN.\nAnd they will not be able to keep away therefrom. \nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(17)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD DEENE.\nAnd what will explain to thee what the Day of Judgment is? \nثُمَّ مَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(18)\nSUMMA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD DEEN.\nAgain, what will explain to thee what the Day of Judgment is? \nيَوْمَ لَا تَمْلِكُ نَفْسٌ لِّنَفْسٍ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَالْاَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ‏(19)\nYAWMA LAA TAMLEKO NAFSUL LE-NAFSIN SHAY-AA, WAL AMRO YAWMA-EZIL LILLAAH.\n(It will be) the Day when no soul shall have power (to do) aught for another: For the command, that Day, will be (wholly) with Allah. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Infetaar (The Cleaving Asunder)\nThere are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that if a person recites this Surah frequently in his prayers then on the Day of Judgement there will be no curtain between Allah (s.w.t.) and himself and when his book of deeds will be opened, Allah (s.w.t.) will protect him from humiliation.\nIf a prisoner writes this Surah and keeps it with him, he will be released sooner and he will be saved from any dangers. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that even if the sins of the one who recites this Surah are equal to the drops of rain, he will still be forgiven. This Surah is also good for the eyes and one should blow gently into the eyes after reciting this Surah."
